.policy "ruff-pyi009-pass-statement-stub-body" revision 2
.description "Use an ellipsis instead of pass as the whole body of a function or class in stub files; stubs only declare types and are never executed."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PYI009 (flake8-pyi), stubs only: a def or class whose whole body is `pass`. A stub writes `...`.
//   def f(): pass          ← PYI009
//   class C:
//       x: int
//       pass               not this rule: PYI012
#include "python/typing.rr"

.violation PYI009(at: node) code "PYI009" "Replace this `pass` with `...`; stub bodies are never executed, so the empty body is written as an ellipsis."
    suppress ruff "PYI009"
PYI009(s) :- (def_body(_, b) ; class_body(_, b)), body_one(b, s), pass_stmt(s), in_stub(s).
